  "result": "Gate verdict: **OK** (3 witnesses, 1 name, 1 atom read), reached on the second of six runs.\n\n**Body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/turning.lean`):\n\n```lean\ndef body : Formula :=\n  .cmp (.abs (.quantity \"prim_heading_change\" [aU] [pWindow])) .ge pHeadingChangeTolerance\n```\n\nThe record's one element maps to `prim.heading_change` with this concept's `window` formal passed\nstraight into the primitive's own window parameter; `abs` is the contract's \"magnitude\" (either\nhand, no direction stated), `.ge` its \"at least\". No narrowings — the contract fixed the quantity,\nthe window and the sense of the bound.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/turning.lean`): one instance with\n`window = 2 s`, `tolerance = 5°`; nine scenes 0.5 s apart in each trace. `holds` — a 20 °/s left\nswing round an intersection, 40° per window; `fails` — reversing straight with 0.4 °/s, 0.8° per\nwindow; `blind` — the same corner with `kin.yaw_rate` masked.\n\n**Gate runs**\n\n1. `WITNESS_FAIL`: the blind episode was unknown for `window_truncated`, not for the masked atom — the 2 s lookback is truncated at every trace's first instants, and no padding can fix the very first observation. Fixed by naming the covered instant range `[2000, 4000] ms` on `blind`, as the other two scenarios already did.\n2. `OK`.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory with the parameter and instant-range choices, and why I stopped. The record needed no changes, so no `dependency_defect.json`.",
